00:00:11.805 --> 00:00:13.867
The Last Light

00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:20.033
Every evening at dusk, Maren climbed the ninety-two steps of the old lighthouse.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:26.092
The stairs curled upward like the inside of a seashell, and her lantern threw long shadows on the stone.

00:00:26.215 --> 00:00:30.324
At the top, she wound the great clockwork and watched the lamp begin to turn.

00:00:28.711 --> 00:00:34.175
[On screen: Jump to a chapter, or click any sentence to start there]

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.217
The Visitor

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:35.842
One stormy night, someone knocked at the lighthouse door.

00:00:34.175 --> 00:01:02.389
[On screen: Narration carries on into the next chapter, and the page follows]

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:40.771
A young man stood on the step, soaked through, holding a box wrapped in oilcloth.

00:00:40.892 --> 00:00:45.851
His boat had lost its rudder near the rocks, he said, and he had followed the light to shore.

00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:50.401
Maren gave him dry clothes, a bowl of soup and a chair by the stove.

00:00:50.543 --> 00:00:55.921
When he finally opened the box, it held a battered radio, and nothing else.

00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:57.420
Morning

00:00:57.537 --> 00:01:01.599
By sunrise the storm had moved on, leaving the harbour bright and still.

